#: Game.Levels.Demo
msgid "Four levels, grammars from three eras of generative syntax, written in one formal\n"
"language. Each grammar is data: categories, a lexicon, rules. The same derivation relation,\n"
"checked by Lean, decides what each grammar generates."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `BareSyntax/Basic.lean`
#. §1: `Deriv`
#. §2: `CanYield`
#. §3: `{{BUILD_VERSION}}`
#: Game
msgid "**The language.** §0: expressions ⟨string, category⟩, rules as partial\n"
"functions, the derivation relation §1, grammaticality §2. Rules come in two forms:\n"
"a domain given as a list of categories (levels 1–2), or a domain given as a decidable condition\n"
"(level 3, where categories are workspaces).\n"
"\n"
"**References.**\n"
"Keenan, E. & Stabler, E. (2003). *Bare Grammar: Lectures on Linguistic Invariants.* CSLI.\n"
"Chomsky, N. (2013). Problems of projection. *Lingua* 130.\n"
"Chomsky, N. (2020). *The UCLA Lectures.*\n"
"Pan, V. J. *Lecture 10: The Minimalist Program* (\\§9).\n"
"\n"
